@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+---
+id: task-004-add-importtasks-bulk-import-helper-to-src-index.ts
+type: task
+title: "Add importTasks bulk-import helper to src/index.ts"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Add a public helper for bulk import, `importTasks(list, text)`, exported from `src/index.ts`. `text`
+holds one task per line as `title;priority;tags`: priority may be left empty for a normal one, tags are
+space-separated, blank lines are skipped. It adds every valid line to `list` and returns
+`{ imported, rejected }`, where `rejected` lists every line that could not be added as
+`{ line, reason }`, `line` counting from 1.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Wrote `test/import.test.ts` first (red: `importTasks` did not exist), covering: a full
+  `title;priority;tags` line, an empty-priority/empty-tags line, a line that omits the trailing fields
+  entirely, blank-line skipping, multi-line counting, an empty-title rejection with its line number, an
+  invalid-priority rejection, a within-batch duplicate-title rejection, a too-many-fields rejection, and
+  that a rejected line adds nothing to the list.
+- Implemented `importTasks`, `ImportResult` and `RejectedLine` in `src/index.ts`. It reads the current
+  time once (`new Date().toISOString()`), splits `text` into lines, skips blank ones, splits each
+  remaining line on `;` (rejecting more than three fields), builds a `NewTask` from the fields (empty
+  priority/tags fields becoming `undefined`/`[]`), and hands it to `list.add`, turning a failed result's
+  `error.message` into the rejected line's `reason`. See
+  `dl-004-bulk-import-reuses-tasklist.add-s-validation-reads-the-clock-once-at-the-index.ts-boundary` for
+  why the clock is read here instead of in `src/domain/`, and why validation is not duplicated.
+- `npm test` is green: 31 tests (21 previous + 10 new), 0 failures.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+None. The feature is additive; no existing signature changed.
